---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../../components/Diagram.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import { page } from "../../lib/nav.ts";

const CHART = "deploy/helm/iki";
const TPL = "deploy/config-template";
const href = (label: string) => page(label).href;
const RELEASES = href("Releases and images");

const boxes = [
  { id: "source", x: 20, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Source", sub: "Wasm as source + SHA-256", href: href("WebAssembly") },
  { id: "deps", x: 250, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Dependency gate", sub: "3 days old; licences", href: href("Dependencies") },
  { id: "live", x: 480, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Live-test gate", sub: "every cloud, the tag", href: href("Live clouds and scale") },
  { id: "publish", x: 710, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "publish.yml", sub: "7 images, signed", strong: true, href: RELEASES },
  { id: "release", x: 710, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "release.yml", sub: "chart, worker, npm", href: RELEASES },
  { id: "config", x: 20, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Config repository", sub: "one per deployment", href: RELEASES },
  { id: "build", x: 250, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Deployment build", sub: "build, sign, approve", strong: true, href: RELEASES },
  { id: "customer", x: 480, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Customer registry", sub: "licensed images", href: href("Licensed images") },
  { id: "infra", x: 20, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "OpenTofu", sub: "GCP and AWS roots", href: href("Cloud infrastructure") },
  { id: "cluster", x: 250, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Cluster", sub: "one Helm chart", strong: true, href: href("The Helm chart") },
  { id: "admit", x: 480, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Admission", sub: "signed or approved", href: RELEASES },
  { id: "workers", x: 710, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Lab workers", sub: "update to signed releases", href: RELEASES },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "source", to: "deps" },
  { from: "deps", to: "live" },
  { from: "live", to: "publish" },
  { from: "publish", to: "release", dashed: true },
  { from: "publish", to: "build", label: "base images, checked" },
  { from: "config", to: "build" },
  { from: "customer", to: "build" },
  { from: "build", to: "cluster", label: "Deploy PR, GitOps" },
  { from: "infra", to: "cluster" },
  { from: "cluster", to: "admit" },
  { from: "release", to: "workers" },
];

const H = {
  short: "How Iki gets from this repository to a lab's cluster",
  how: "From a tagged release to admitted pods",
  ref: "Where, and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      Each organization gets its own deployment on Kubernetes, from one Helm chart. Iki publishes
      signed images with provenance and SBOMs, but only after a live deployment to every cloud has
      passed for the tag. A deployment is a git repository of its own: its CI builds the pinned
      plugins onto Iki's images, signs the result, approves the images its runs may use, and opens a
      pull request whose merge is the deploy. In the cluster, run pods are admitted only if Iki
      signed their image or the deployment approved it. Reference OpenTofu sets up Google Cloud or
      AWS around the chart.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Single-tenant deployments on Kubernetes, with Helm (<Adr n={[2, 14]} />).</li>
      <li>GitOps configuration per deployment (<Adr n="0015" />).</li>
      <li>Signed, attested artifacts verified at deploy time (<Adr n={[17, 63]} />).</li>
      <li>Deployments supply licensed images Iki doesn't ship (<Adr n="0209" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <Diagram id="deploy" title="From Iki's release to a lab's cluster" width={920} height={350} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="source">
        <p>No <code>.wasm</code> file is ever in git: the Rust source and a SHA-256 for each module are.</p>
        <p><Path p="server/iki_wasm.wasm.sha256" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="deps">
        <p>Nothing released less than three days ago is locked; vulnerabilities and licences are checked (<Adr n={[17, 19]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="scripts/supply-chain/check-deps.sh" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="live">
        <p>Both the publish and release workflows refuse a tag until each cloud's live test has passed at it.</p>
        <p><Path p="deploy/live/live_runs.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="publish">
        <p>The server, the worker and five first-party tool images, scanned, signed and attested (<Adr n={[17, 65]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p=".github/workflows/publish.yml" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="release">
        <p>The chart, the worker's binaries, and two npm packages, signed (<Adr n="0017" />).</p>
        <p><Path p=".github/workflows/release.yml" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="config">
        <p>One folder per deployment: the Iki version, images by digest, plugins, values and settings (<Adr n={[15, 34]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={TPL} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="build">
        <p>The deployment's CI builds its images, signs them, approves the images runs use, and opens a Deploy pull request (<Adr n={[34, 63]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={`${TPL}/.github/workflows/build.yml`} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="customer">
        <p>A licensed image the lab supplies, bound to an environment and a range of plugin releases (<Adr n="0209" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/compute.py" sym="class ImageBinding" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="infra">
        <p>Reference OpenTofu for Google Cloud and AWS, with an output of chart values (<Adr n={[97, 107, 109]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="deploy/gcp/production" />, <Path p="deploy/aws/production" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="cluster">
        <p>Web, tasks, the migrate hook, workers, the provisioner, the egress proxy and network policies (<Adr n={[14, 53, 155]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={`${CHART}/templates`} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="admit">
        <p>A Sigstore policy on the pods the provisioner makes: Iki's signature or the deployment's approval (<Adr n="0063" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={`${CHART}/templates/image-policy.yaml`} sym="kind: ClusterImagePolicy" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="workers">
        <p>Workers on people's computers update themselves to releases Iki signed (<Adr n="0060" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="worker/crates/iki-worker/src/update.rs" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>
    <p>Which page covers each part:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><PageLink to="Releases and images" />: what a tagged release publishes, how it's signed, a deployment's config repository and build, and what the cluster admits.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="The Helm chart" />: what runs in the cluster.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Cloud infrastructure" />: the OpenTofu for Google Cloud and AWS.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Licensed images" />: images a deployment supplies for licensed tools.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Dependencies" />: the minimum release age, licences and vulnerabilities.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="The dev cluster" />: the same chart on a laptop, and in CI.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="WebAssembly" /> and <PageLink to="Live clouds and scale" />: the Wasm modules, and the live tests a release waits for.</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={CHART} />: the chart</li>
        <li><Path p={TPL} />: a deployment's config repository</li>
        <li><Path p="deploy/gcp" />, <Path p="deploy/aws" />: reference infrastructure</li>
        <li><Path p="docs/supply-chain.md" />: verifying what Iki publishes</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0002" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0014" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0015" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0017" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0063" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
